{
    "version": "https://jsonfeed.org/version/1",
    "title": "NixOS Package PRs for gnused-4.9, sddm, nano, agenix, e2fsprogs-1.46.6, breeze-gtk packages",
    "home_page_url": "https://pbek.github.io/github-search-rss/nixos-packages-53.json",
    "feed_url": "https://pbek.github.io/github-search-rss/nixos-packages-53.json",
    "description": "NixOS Package PRs for gnused-4.9, sddm, nano, agenix, e2fsprogs-1.46.6, breeze-gtk packages on GitHub",
    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124387056?u=dd1822b010c60120060b388310cd5749a87aced1&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR introduces a <code class=\"notranslate\">sddm.themePackage</code> option to simplify SDDM theme installation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #354834.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2646485839\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/354834\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/354834/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/354834\">#354834</a></p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Problems with <code class=\"notranslate\">sddm.theme</code>:</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To install an sddm theme a user previously had to go through these steps:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Find out the theme <code class=\"notranslate\">Name</code> by manually inspecting <code class=\"notranslate\">metadata.desktop</code> or reading the package homepage for <a href=\"https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.05&amp;from=0&amp;size=50&amp;sort=relevance&amp;type=packages&amp;query=sddm+theme\" rel=\"nofollow\">services.displayManager.sddm.theme</a></li>\n<li>Install the theme package to <a href=\"https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.05&amp;from=0&amp;size=50&amp;sort=relevance&amp;type=packages&amp;query=environment+systemPackages\" rel=\"nofollow\">environment.systemPackages</a>, so that SDDM finds it in <code class=\"notranslate\">share/sddm/themes</code></li>\n<li>Add the theme package to <a href=\"https://search.nixos.org/options?query=extraPackages%20sddm&amp;channel=25.05\" rel=\"nofollow\">services.displayManager.sddm.extraPackages</a>, so that SDDM is able to access its Qt dependencies\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Alternatively the package has to use <code class=\"notranslate\">$out/nix-support/propagated-user-env-packages</code>, which (as I understand it) bloats the global environment</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To customize the theme one has to go through another lengthy (and undocumented) procedure.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Inspect the theme nix source to find out if it has overrides that allow customization. Now there are a few options</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The theme doesn't expose any overrides - You're screwed and can't customize the theme unless you patch <code class=\"notranslate\">nixpkgs</code></li>\n<li>The theme only exposes some overrides such as <code class=\"notranslate\">Background</code> - You can partially customize the theme</li>\n<li>The theme exposes a override with a non-standardized name (<code class=\"notranslate\">themeConfig</code>) that lets you properly customize the theme</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In any way a manual inspection of the nix package source is necessary</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To select a different theme flavor the process is similar. You have to check for overrides in the nix package.<br>\nThe options have inconsistent names such as <code class=\"notranslate\">embededTheme</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">flavor</code> or are not exposed at all (you can't select a flavor)<br>\nAcross all themes there is never any integrity checking whether a flavor is valid.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">How this PR addresses those Problems</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR tries to solve this by introducing the <code class=\"notranslate\">sddm.themePackage</code> option which automatically does all of those steps for you.<br>\nA new <code class=\"notranslate\">buildSddmThemePackage</code> builder is added that simplifies maintaining and adding new SDDM themes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">propagatedBuildInputs</code> are renamed to <code class=\"notranslate\">sddmBuildInputs</code> and used in <a href=\"https://search.nixos.org/options?query=extraPackages%20sddm&amp;channel=25.05\" rel=\"nofollow\">services.displayManager.sddm.extraPackages</a> directly.<br>\nThe path to the config file has to be specified in the builder, meaning that it can be overwritten automatically for every package. The builder exposes a passthru that allows editing the theme.<br>\nThe old overrides (<code class=\"notranslate\">themeConfig</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">background</code>, ...) still work but print a deprecation warning.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Other advantages of this approach</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A <code class=\"notranslate\">buildSddmThemePackage</code> builder makes SDDM themes more standardized and new documentation will make it way easier to package new SDDM themes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The builder exposes a <code class=\"notranslate\">testGreeter</code> that makes testing themes way easier.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Packaging a theme</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See the <a href=\"https://github.com/DaniD3v/nixpkgs/blob/sddm-themePackage/doc/packages/sddm.section.md\"><code class=\"notranslate\">buildSddmThemePackage</code> docs</a>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Open Questions</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Should we parse <code class=\"notranslate\">meta.license</code> from <code class=\"notranslate\">metadata.desktop</code> automatically?</li>\n<li>Should there be a <code class=\"notranslate\">sddmThemes</code> package set at the cost of not using <code class=\"notranslate\">by-name</code>?</li>\n<li>Should the remaining Qt 6 themes be ported here or by their maintainers in follow-ups? <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/romildo/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/romildo\">@romildo</a> (<code class=\"notranslate\">qogir-kde</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">utterly-nord-plasma</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">whitesur-kde</code>), <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/khaneliman/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/khaneliman\">@khaneliman</a> (<code class=\"notranslate\">catppuccin-sddm-corners</code>)</li>\n<li>Should the src stay a separate derivation?<br>\nI think its cleaner but maybe 2 derivations are bad?</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Discussion</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">buildSddmThemePackage</code> sets <code class=\"notranslate\">dontConfigure</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">dontBuild</code>, so themes that need a build step (<code class=\"notranslate\">catppuccin-sddm</code>) use a nested <code class=\"notranslate\">src</code> derivation. This makes them harder to override.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">kdePackages.sddm-theme-breeze</code> needs <code class=\"notranslate\">plasma-workspace</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">sddmBuildInputs</code>, which grows the greeter closure from 697 MiB to 2.8 GiB. A separate output for its QML modules would fix this, but that's up to the KDE team.</li>\n<li>The code blocks in the docs aren't tested. <code class=\"notranslate\">nixosTests.sddm</code> could use <code class=\"notranslate\">elegant-sddm.withConfig { ... }</code> to cover them.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">PR Status</h2>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Core functionality</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> basic <code class=\"notranslate\">sddmBuildThemePackage</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">testGreeter</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">passthru</code> of <code class=\"notranslate\">sddmBuildThemePackage</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">withConfig</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">passthru</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">themePackage</code> module</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> add sanity checks to find <code class=\"notranslate\">metadata.desktop</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">theme.conf</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> remove <code class=\"notranslate\">sddm.theme</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Porting packages</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Qt 6:</p>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">catppuccin-sddm</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">elegant-sddm</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">sddm-astronaut</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">where-is-my-sddm-theme</code> (Qt 5 variant dropped)</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">kdePackages.sddm-theme-breeze</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">sddm.themes.{elarun,maldives,maui,maya}</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">catppuccin-sddm-corners</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">qogir-kde</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">utterly-nord-plasma</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">whitesur-kde</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Many of the unpackaged themes have an annoying <code class=\"notranslate\">install.sh</code> script that needs to be patched because it copies to <code class=\"notranslate\">/usr/share</code> and requires root.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Testing</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Run the <code class=\"notranslate\">testGreeter</code> with all SDDM themes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">AI disclosure: in the commits with an <code class=\"notranslate\">Assisted-by:</code> trailer, individual hunks were proposed by AI, then manually edited and approved.</p>\n\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Fits <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md\">pkgs/README.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/maintainers/README.md\">maintainers/README.md</a> and other READMEs.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Follows the <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#automationai-policy\">automation/AI policy</a>.</li>\n<li>Built on platform:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Tested, as applicable:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Basic functionality of all binary files, usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Ran <code class=\"notranslate\">nixpkgs-review</code> on this PR. See <a href=\"https://github.com/Mic92/nixpkgs-review#usage\">nixpkgs-review usage</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md#package-tests\">Package tests</a> at <code class=\"notranslate\">passthru.tests</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/index.html#sec-nixos-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">NixOS tests</a> in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/tests\">nixos/tests</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tests in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/lib/tests\">lib/tests</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/test\">pkgs/test</a> for functions and \"core\" functionality.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Nixpkgs Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Package update: when the change is major or breaking.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>NixOS Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module addition: when adding a new NixOS module.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Module update: when the change is significant.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
