        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34915973?u=5b32114f1bbded01bc07cbe833dd86939347e92c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h6 dir=\"auto\">Motivation for this change</h6>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The SDDM display manager wants access to the <code class=\"notranslate\">.face.icon</code> files stored in user home directories. Currently, this is not possible because <code class=\"notranslate\">systemd-tmpfiles</code> resets the access permissions for home directories of users with <code class=\"notranslate\">createHome = true</code> every reboot.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR simply gives SDDM the required access rights for all \"normal\" users.</p>\n<h6 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h6>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li>Built on platform(s)\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-darwin</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> For non-Linux: Is <code class=\"notranslate\">sandbox = true</code> set in <code class=\"notranslate\">nix.conf</code>? (See <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nix/stable/command-ref/conf-file.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Nix manual</a>)</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Tested, as applicable:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/index.html#sec-nixos-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">NixOS test(s)</a> (look inside <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/tests\">nixos/tests</a>)</li>\n<li>and/or <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixpkgs/unstable/#sec-package-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">package tests</a></li>\n<li>or, for functions and \"core\" functionality, tests in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/lib/tests\">lib/tests</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/test\">pkgs/test</a></li>\n<li>made sure NixOS tests are <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixpkgs/unstable/#ssec-nixos-tests-linking\" rel=\"nofollow\">linked</a> to the relevant packages</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tested compilation of all packages that depend on this change using <code class=\"notranslate\">nix-shell -p nixpkgs-review --run \"nixpkgs-review rev HEAD\"</code>. Note: all changes have to be committed, also see <a href=\"https://github.com/Mic92/nixpkgs-review#usage\">nixpkgs-review usage</a></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Tested basic functionality of all binary files (usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#generating-2205-release-notes\">22.05 Release Notes (or backporting 21.11 Release notes)</a>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Package updates) Added a release notes entry if the change is major or breaking</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Module updates) Added a release notes entry if the change is significant</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Module addition) Added a release notes entry if adding a new NixOS module</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Release notes changes) Ran <code class=\"notranslate\">nixos/doc/manual/md-to-db.sh</code> to update generated release notes</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Fits <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/154152",
            "title": "nixos/sddm: Grant SDDM access to icons in home directories",
            "date_modified": "2024-07-04T15:09:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2022-01-09T15:33:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "leotaku",
                "url": "https://github.com/leotaku"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49513131?u=941f372645cb79b087f7418ce94f0c340e135a6c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">nordic was using the qt5 packages <code class=\"notranslate\">plasma-framework</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">plasma-workspace</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">breeze-icons</code>.<br>\nPlasma 5 and its packages (including <code class=\"notranslate\">plasma-workspace</code>) are scheduled for removal until 25.11.<br>\nDepending on these qt5 packages is probelamtic and will break.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is ignoring the fact it is also probably broken logic in the first place. If sddm needs packages to be themeable, those should then be part of the sddm module, if anything. Adding them to the theme package is silly.</p>\n\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li>Built on platform(s)\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-darwin</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>For non-Linux: Is sandboxing enabled in <code class=\"notranslate\">nix.conf</code>? (See <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nix/stable/command-ref/conf-file.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Nix manual</a>)\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">sandbox = relaxed</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">sandbox = true</code></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tested, as applicable:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/index.html#sec-nixos-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">NixOS test(s)</a> (look inside <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/tests\">nixos/tests</a>)</li>\n<li>and/or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md#package-tests\">package tests</a></li>\n<li>or, for functions and \"core\" functionality, tests in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/lib/tests\">lib/tests</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/test\">pkgs/test</a></li>\n<li>made sure NixOS tests are <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md#linking-nixos-module-tests-to-a-package\">linked</a> to the relevant packages</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tested compilation of all packages that depend on this change using <code class=\"notranslate\">nix-shell -p nixpkgs-review --run \"nixpkgs-review rev HEAD\"</code>. Note: all changes have to be committed, also see <a href=\"https://github.com/Mic92/nixpkgs-review#usage\">nixpkgs-review usage</a></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tested basic functionality of all binary files (usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/doc/release-notes/rl-2511.section.md\">Nixpkgs 25.11 Release Notes</a> (or backporting <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/doc/release-notes/rl-2411.section.md\">24.11</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2505.section.md\">25.05</a> Nixpkgs Release notes)\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Package updates) Added a release notes entry if the change is major or breaking</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2511.section.md\">NixOS 25.11 Release Notes</a> (or backporting <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2411.section.md\">24.11</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2505.section.md\">25.05</a> NixOS Release notes)\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Module updates) Added a release notes entry if the change is significant</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Module addition) Added a release notes entry if adding a new NixOS module</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Fits <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add a 👍 <a href=\"https://github.blog/2016-03-10-add-reactions-to-pull-requests-issues-and-comments/\" rel=\"nofollow\">reaction</a> to <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pulls?q=is%3Aopen+sort%3Areactions-%2B1-desc\">pull requests you find important</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/410922",
            "title": "nordic: remove broken sddm \"propagation\"",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-23T23:13:32.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-05-25T20:50:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "GrimmTheShrimp",
                "url": "https://github.com/GrimmTheShrimp"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27977196?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Moved the line setting <code class=\"notranslate\">EDITOR</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">nano</code> out of nixos/environment into nixos/nano so that it is only set when it's available on the system. Tried to stay consistent with nixos/vim.<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">nano.defaultEditor</code> defaults to <code class=\"notranslate\">nano.enable</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> so that there won't be an error in current configs if <code class=\"notranslate\">nano.enable</code> is <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> while still throwing an error if the former is explicitly set to <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> while the latter to <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li>Built on platform:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-darwin</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Tested, as applicable:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/index.html#sec-nixos-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">NixOS tests</a> in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/tests\">nixos/tests</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md#package-tests\">Package tests</a> at <code class=\"notranslate\">passthru.tests</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tests in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/lib/tests\">lib/tests</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/test\">pkgs/test</a> for functions and \"core\" functionality.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Ran <code class=\"notranslate\">nixpkgs-review</code> on this PR. See <a href=\"https://github.com/Mic92/nixpkgs-review#usage\">nixpkgs-review usage</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tested basic functionality of all binary files, usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>.</li>\n<li>Nixpkgs Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Package update: when the change is major or breaking.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>NixOS Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module addition: when adding a new NixOS module.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module update: when the change is significant.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Fits <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md\">pkgs/README.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/maintainers/README.md\">maintainers/README.md</a> and other READMEs.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add a 👍 <a href=\"https://github.blog/2016-03-10-add-reactions-to-pull-requests-issues-and-comments/\" rel=\"nofollow\">reaction</a> to <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pulls?q=is%3Aopen+sort%3Areactions-%2B1-desc\">pull requests you find important</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/463568",
            "title": "nixos/nano: refactor EDITOR out of nixos/environment",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-23T14:41:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-20T22:03:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "TheSast",
                "url": "https://github.com/TheSast"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78693624?u=28ec3a9fc54094fb3c590cfb9cf80600076b5ec9&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Other editors like vim and emacs provide an option defaultEditor, which automatically sets the environment variable $EDITOR to use that editor by default. This brings similar functionality to nano.</p>\n\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li>Built on platform(s)\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-darwin</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>For non-Linux: Is sandboxing enabled in <code class=\"notranslate\">nix.conf</code>? (See <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nix/stable/command-ref/conf-file.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Nix manual</a>)\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">sandbox = relaxed</code></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <code class=\"notranslate\">sandbox = true</code></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tested, as applicable:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/index.html#sec-nixos-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">NixOS test(s)</a> (look inside <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/tests\">nixos/tests</a>)</li>\n<li>and/or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md#package-tests\">package tests</a></li>\n<li>or, for functions and \"core\" functionality, tests in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/lib/tests\">lib/tests</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/test\">pkgs/test</a></li>\n<li>made sure NixOS tests are <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixpkgs/unstable/#ssec-nixos-tests-linking\" rel=\"nofollow\">linked</a> to the relevant packages</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tested compilation of all packages that depend on this change using <code class=\"notranslate\">nix-shell -p nixpkgs-review --run \"nixpkgs-review rev HEAD\"</code>. Note: all changes have to be committed, also see <a href=\"https://github.com/Mic92/nixpkgs-review#usage\">nixpkgs-review usage</a></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tested basic functionality of all binary files (usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2411.section.md\">24.11 Release Notes</a> (or backporting <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2311.section.md\">23.11</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2405.section.md\">24.05</a> Release notes)\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Package updates) Added a release notes entry if the change is major or breaking</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Module updates) Added a release notes entry if the change is significant</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> (Module addition) Added a release notes entry if adding a new NixOS module</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Fits <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add a 👍 <a href=\"https://github.blog/2016-03-10-add-reactions-to-pull-requests-issues-and-comments/\" rel=\"nofollow\">reaction</a> to <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pulls?q=is%3Aopen+sort%3Areactions-%2B1-desc\">pull requests you find important</a>.</p>",
